// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Diablo Research
// Date: 2026-10-04 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Detects the Microsoft XML Schema Definition Tool "xsd.exe" loading input from a remote HTTP or
//   HTTPS location. Adversaries may abuse this behavior to retrieve remote content using a
//   Microsoft-signed developer utility.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of Xsd.exe with remote XML or schema resources by developers
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/serialization/xml-schema-definition-tool-xsd-exe
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/blob/a79893e7ad7fe69e9eeb37c82e90685e10663312/yml/OtherMSBinaries/xsd.yml
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/2a2bb5284c15792e5b07190ad35ff81f1b7988d9/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_xsd_remote_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\xsd.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "xsd.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://")
